F = {
"bg|Gate Warden": "You lived for a long time near a portal or in a place steeped in planar energy, like a gatetown in the Outlands. Sights that terrify or dazzle other people feel ordinary to you. You deal with Celestials and Fiends as easily as with any shopkeeper.",
"bg|Genie Touched": "Genie magic still lingers in your homeland, and one day your life crossed paths with a genie. It may have been a djinni in a lamp, a marid at an oasis, a dao, or an efreeti. The meeting left you sharp-eyed, smooth-tongued, and a little magical.",
"bg|Giant Foundling": "You are not a Giant, yet giants raised you, or you grew up in a land full of huge creatures. Some magic in your surroundings made you unusually large. You learned to channel giant strength, and you see the world from the viewpoint of someone used to towering neighbors.",
"bg|Golgari Agent": "You belong to the Golgari swarm, one small piece of a vast living system of decay and renewal. You grew up in the dark corners of the city where life's messy side shows. You feel no fear of death or the dead, only a fierce respect for the cycle.",
"bg|Grinner": "You are a Grinner of the Golden Grin, a secret network that began in Tal'Dorei and now operates from hidden bases across the Clovis Concord. Your group works to reach the top of the Dwendalian Empire. You aim to bring freedom and hope to the oppressed, and spread coded folk songs to warn allies.",
"bg|Gruul Anarch": "You come from the wild fringes of Ravnica, the ruined districts, rubble fields, and overgrown parks left outside the great city. Your people cling to the Old Ways and live close to nature and primal fury. The rest of the world, busy with progress, pays you little attention.",
"bg|Guard": "You spent long hours on watch in a tower, and your feet still remember it. You were trained to look two ways at once. One eye scanned beyond the wall for raiders from the forest, and the other searched inside for thieves and troublemakers.",
"bg|Guide": "You grew up in the open wilderness, and home was wherever you laid your bedroll. You explored strange monsters, clean forests and streams, and old ruins built by giants. Along the way you led friendly nature priests, who taught you the basics of wild magic.",
"bg|Guild Artisan": "You belong to an artisan guild and work closely with other crafters in your trade. Your skill and wealth put you in the merchant class, free from feudal duties. You trained as an apprentice under a master, with your guild's backing, until you earned the rank of master yourself.",
"bg|Harper": "You accepted an invitation to join the Harpers and swore to follow their code and serve the common good. You know when to work as a team and when to act alone. Veteran Harpers taught you secret melodies, watchwords, and sleight of hand to watch and thwart evil.",
"bg|Haunted One": "Your past haunts you, whether it came from one terrible event or a long run of pain. You have tried burying it and running from it, and nothing worked. No sword can cut it down and no spell can banish it, yet you keep going.",
"bg|Hermit": "You spent a formative stretch of your life apart from society, either in a sheltered community like a monastery or completely alone. Away from the noise of the world, you found stillness and solitude. You may also have found some of the answers you were seeking.",
"bg|Horizon Weaver Initiate": "As a restless teenager you left home as soon as you could and went traveling. On the road you met the Horizon Weavers, adventurous conjurers. They taught you some of their teleportation magic to help you explore farther.",
"bg|House Agent": "You are tied to a dragonmarked house but have not yet shown a dragonmark. You may be family by blood or simply an employee. Your work has been running the house's business as the eyes, hands, and feet of its leaders, and you have friends, mentors, and rivals inside it and beyond.",
"bg|House Cannith Heir": "You are a scion of House Cannith, which builds the marvels of the modern age. The house expects you to add to its success through invention, study, business, or diplomacy. A deep split inside the house troubles you, as three barons compete for leadership and you probably favor one.",
"bg|House Deneith Heir": "As an heir of House Deneith you trained for battle, though you neither chase it nor fear it. You value duty, honor, and the laws that serve when those fail. You may have guarded a minor dignitary, fought as a mercenary, or hunted fugitives as a marshal. You expect your due place in the house.",
"bg|House Ghallanda Heir": "House Ghallanda raised you among comfort, good talk, fine drink, and tasty meals. You might be a witty, charming host who loves a warm hearth, or a schemer who uses trust to bend others. Adventure may let you learn foreign cuisines, grow your contacts, or save up for your own inn.",
"bg|House Jorasco Heir": "House Jorasco teaches that sickness and wounds haunt the living and steal health and long life. You learned to fight them with magic and medicine, and to make sure you are paid well. You might be a gentle healer who avoids battle, or a cold specialist who knows exactly how to disable or kill.",
"bg|House Kundarak Heir": "You are proud of your Kundarak family and its work guarding the valuables of Khorvaire. The house leads among the clans of the Mror Holds and is known for professionalism, honor, and order. You may uphold that name, put your own honor first, or rebel against what the house demands.",
"bg|House Lyrandar Heir": "As a Lyrandar heir, you count the wind as an ally and the sea and sky as your realm. Your house is rising thanks to its airship mastery. You may have worked as a sailor, navigator, shipwright, Raincaller, or airship crew, and the house may send you after pirates or ruins.",
"bg|House Medani Heir": "Your life as a Medani heir centers on intrigue, but your job is stopping it. You see the world as a web of schemes and counterplots, and you use instinct to spot threats to your clients early. Your house prefers that no blade is ever drawn, rather than blocking one afterward.",
"bg|House Orien Heir": "House Orien once connected Khorvaire with trade roads and lightning rails. The Last War broke those links and ended Galifar. Couriers still carry goods, and the house wants routes across the Mournland restored. Orien adventurers look into missing couriers, stolen caravan cargo, and trouble on the lightning rail.",
"bg|House Phiarlan Heir": "You grew up with wealth, fame, and beauty in House Phiarlan, yet you value knowledge and the power it gives most of all. You may be a performer or artist who listens for secrets while entertaining crowds. You may instead link up with the house's spy branch, the Serpentine Table.",
"bg|House Sivis Heir": "Your family has spent almost three thousand years keeping order, because communication holds civilization together. Your ancestors settled royal disputes and helped dragonmarked houses find their place. While other houses chase fame, Sivis plays a quiet, long game of influence behind the scenes and shapes the age.",
"bg|House Tharashk Heir": "Other heirs live in luxury, but House Tharashk taught you to rely on yourself. The young house has little wealth and plenty of drive, and it has a destiny you share. In battle or conversation you act as a hunter who studies foes, finds weaknesses, and wins by any means.",
"bg|House Thuranni Heir": "House Thuranni is young and built on espionage, so its leaders expect you to advance its interests whenever you can. Everything you did as the house found its footing was watched closely. Even the quietest artist or artisan in the house follows politics and passes along information when asked.",
"bg|House Vadalis Heir": "You grew up valuing both family and nature. You know how the Five Nations live but stay out of their games of status and ambition. You understand life's power and its mysteries, and your feel for nature lets you see through city folk's deceit without ever showing it.",
"bg|Ice Fisher": "You come from a proud line of ice fishers in Ten-Towns, Icewind Dale. Pulling knucklehead trout from frozen lakes is not glamorous, but it pays honestly. You learned to sense the faintest tug on a line, and the hard work toughened your body and mind for adventuring.",
"bg|Inheritor": "You are the heir to something precious, though not money. A single object was entrusted to you, perhaps by family, a friend, or a mentor. Learning of it changed your life and may have launched your adventures. It also brings danger from those who want to take it from you.",
"bg|Initiate": "You are an initiate working through the trials of the five gods, hoping for a glorious death in the final Trial of Zeal. Your talents and teachers pointed you toward close combat, ranged combat, or spellcasting. A truly worthy initiate stays well rounded, so multiclassing or feats can fill the gaps.",
"bg|Inquisitive": "Boundless curiosity drives you, and you sharpened your skills of investigation and deduction to solve mysteries, find missing people, recover stolen goods, and expose corruption and conspiracies. You may have worked freelance, for an inquisitive agency such as one licensed by House Medani or Tharashk, for a newspaper, or for the police.",
"bg|Inquisitor": "Inquisitors were once cathar detectives who looked into both ordinary and supernatural crimes, often in remote parishes, and who unmasked hidden werewolves. While Avacyn was trapped in the Helvault, they became brutal, executing suspects and holding unsanctioned trials. After her madness, that cruelty became normal, and the true investigators are now few.",
"bg|Investigator": "You pursue the truth without rest. You may have seen something strange or awful and need to understand it, or you may simply care about justice and honesty. Whether the case is a local crime or an eldritch conspiracy, you work to expose what others want hidden.",
"bg|Izzet Engineer": "You bring an inventive mind, a love of magical technology, and endless energy to the research of the Izzet League. You likely start as an attendant, but you might rise to mage, alchemist, lab supervisor, or flamethrower-carrying scorchbringer. You embody the Izzet spirit of brilliant, obsessive, chaotic inspiration.",
"bg|Knight of Solamnia": "You trained as a Knight of Solamnia, a valorous warrior. Strict rules shape everything you do, and you work to follow them while protecting the weak and opposing evil. Honor matters to you as much as your own life.",
"bg|Knight of the Gauntlet": "You did not want to spend your days reading scripture in a quiet temple, so you joined the Order of the Gauntlet as a holy warrior. You scorn evil, stand by your fellow knights, and care for survivors of war. You swore to rest only when justice outshines chaos across Faerun.",
"bg|Knight of the Order": "You belong to a knightly order sworn to a vital cause. Faerun has many such orders, and most welcome all kinds of folk who will fight and die for the goal, not just armored nobles. Some serve a god, some a government, and others follow a philosophy.",
"bg|Lords' Alliance Vassal": "You swore loyalty to a member city of the Lords' Alliance and pledged to increase safety and prosperity along the Sword Coast. You bring honor to your lord's house, whether by guarding trade roads for a Waterdeep merchant-lord or hunting monsters near Daggerford. You are as skilled with a sword as with a quill.",
"bg|Lorehold Student": "You spent your youth preparing for Lorehold College and read every book on its list for applicants. History is your great passion. You might dream of using magic to speak with famous figures of the past or your own ancestors, or to recreate the mighty magic of a distant era.",
"bg|Lorwyn Expert": "You come from Lorwyn, the land of endless sunshine, or you have studied it closely. You see the creature Eirdu as the living sun and love whimsical adventures. You cherish loved ones, having watched some wander into Shadowmoor and fade. You stay brave and eager for new experiences.",
"bg|Luxonborn (Acolyte)": "Every acolyte serves a god, but you serve the Luxon, whom you believe stands above godhood and made the cosmos. You study potential, which the Luxon embodies. Your Shelter of the Faithful feature covers all who revere the Luxon and all who practice dunamancy, the art it gave the world.",
"bg|Mage of High Sorcery": "The Mages of High Sorcery noticed your magical talent, and you trained with this group that studies magic and prevents its misuse. You may yet face the dangerous test for full membership. Your passion likely leans you toward the White, Red, or Black Robes. They accept sorcerers and warlocks too.",
"bg|Marine": "You trained to fight on sandy beaches and rocky shores. You led midnight raids from fast ships whose names frighten your enemies. The sea is your second home, rain is your shelter, and crashing waves are your battle cry.",
"bg|Mercenary Veteran": "You fought battles for coin and know the risk of life and limb for a share of treasure. Now you hope for greater rewards as an adventurer, or for freedom to pick your own work. You have gripping battlefield tales, maybe from the Zhentarim, Mintarn's soldiers, or a small band.",
"bg|Merchant": "You apprenticed with a trader, caravan master, or shopkeeper and learned how commerce works. You traveled widely, buying and selling raw materials for crafters or their finished goods. You may have moved cargo by ship, wagon, or caravan, or kept a shop of your own.",
"bg|Mist Wanderer": "You once had a home, until the Mists rose and pulled you into a Domain of Dread. Since then you have drifted from domain to domain, braving the shifting Mists in search of a way back. The cursed realms changed you, but fellow wanderers offer comfort.",
"bg|Moonwell Pilgrim": "You grew up in the Moonshae Isles, honoring the blessed land, its gods, and the shrines called moonwells. You set out on a pilgrimage to visit and commune with every moonwell. On the way you gathered folk songs, painted lovely vistas, and picked up a bit of primal magic.",
"bg|Mulhorandi Tomb Raider": "You grew up under living god-kings, hearing tales of ancient empires and buried cities full of forgotten treasure. You decided to explore the crypts, tombs, and pyramids of your homeland yourself. Your goal is to reclaim your people's relics from those who are cunning and brave enough to seek them.",
"bg|Mutated Commuter": "You rode a gloomy train to work each day until it crashed. You crawled out of the wreck unhurt but changed, your body mutated by the supernatural violence. You woke near Mordenheim Kinetics, surrounded by sea and misty forest, and entered its campus seeking help, though hope there is thin.",
"bg|Myriad Operative (Criminal)": "You are no common cutpurse. You belong to the Myriad, the greatest crime syndicate in Exandria, with bases in every major city outside Eastern Wynandir. You have criminal contacts and allies, but also rivals and bosses who would sacrifice you. Anywhere the Myriad operates, you can find shelter from the law for a price.",
"bg|Mythalkeeper": "Mythals are great magical powers that can reshape the Weave and even reality. Most are ancient, and many are damaged or dormant. You come from the Dalelands, where you likely met your first mythal in Myth Drannor. You travel Faerun seeking other ruined places of power, to learn their history or repair them.",
"bg|Noble": "You know wealth, power, and privilege. Your family holds a noble title, land, and political sway. You might be a pampered aristocrat, a newly raised merchant, a disinherited scoundrel, or a caring landowner who feels responsible for your people. Work with your DM to shape your title and family.",
"bg|Orzhov Representative": "The Orzhov Syndicate promises immense wealth and moves money from Ravnican society up to the top of its hierarchy. As a low-ranking functionary, you hope to keep as much as you can from the money passing through your hands. That is how you plan to climb until you prove your value.",
"bg|Outlander": "You grew up in the wilds, far from towns and technology. You saw herds bigger than forests, endured weather no city dweller could imagine, and loved being the only thinking creature for miles. The wild runs in your blood, whether you were a nomad, explorer, hermit, hunter, or raider.",
"bg|Phantasmic Circus Trouper": "You found a home with the Phantasmic Circus, as a performer or a circus hand. You traveled the world bringing magic and wonder to eager crowds. In that life you learned some illusion magic and sharpened your talent for performance and misdirection.",
"bg|Plaintiff": "Accidents seem to follow Acquisitions Incorporated operatives. You were left barely alive by one such incident, which a magistrate blamed on the company. Before the ruling, they offered you a job and promised training in swordplay or spellcasting. You left your old life behind, signed the paperwork, and joined up for adventure.",
"bg|Planar Philosopher": "You follow a philosophy that seeks to explain the planes or some hidden truth of the multiverse. Your conviction gives you strength, and you may draw on a network of like-minded thinkers, such as the factions of Sigil. You explore your ideas as you travel and spread them everywhere.",
"bg|Prismari Student": "You are an artist preparing to practice your craft in the tradition of Prismari College. Your medium could be sculpture, dance, painting, music, drama, or architecture. You dream of fusing magic with creativity and bringing your grand artistic visions to life.",
"bg|Purple Dragon Squire": "You pledged yourself to protect Cormyr and hope to join the Purple Dragon Knights, an elite order. First you must serve as a knight's squire, and you found a liege to teach you their ways. You must prove yourself worthy of the order's ideals of glory, honor, and strength.",
"bg|Quandrix Student": "You prepared for Quandrix College by solving its math problems for applicants over many years. You are drawn to the numbers and patterns that run through the natural world. You may lean toward mathematics or physics, or toward abstract studies in metaphysics, arcana, or logic.",
"bg|Rakdos Cultist": "You are a born performer who loves drama and the spotlight, and you honed your demanding skills until they look easy. You live for roaring applause and chaos in the streets. You also belong to a cult of Rakdos, a demon who loves violence and a good show, and you want to please him.",
"bg|Rashemi Wanderer": "You wandered for years across the highlands of Rashemen, a harsh, windy heath dotted with ancient obelisks that imprison Fiends. Dragons, gnolls, and other deadly creatures live there. Friends are rare in such a lonely land, so you learned to keep strangers at arm's length.",
"bg|Reconstructed Runaway": "You believed you had died. You awoke with your mind intact, saved as a perfect neuroprint, but in an artificial body built in the laboratories of Mordenheim Kinetics. The surgery carries a price you cannot or will not pay. To build a new life, you must escape the company that made you.",
"bg|Revelry Pirate (Sailor)": "On the Menagerie Coast nearly everyone sails, but no pirates are as organized or infamous as the Revelry. You serve the Plank King and send him a share of your plunder on Darktow. If you left the crew, watch your back, since the Revelry punishes deserters until they pay up or prove too dangerous.",
"bg|Rewarded": "Your life was hard until a miraculous stroke of luck changed your fate. A kind deity may have granted your deepest wish, you may have drawn a powerful card from a Deck of Many Things, or a distant relative may have left you a fortune. You left your misery behind for adventure.",
"bg|Rival Intern": "You interned at a rival of Acquisitions Incorporated and came to admire its ruthless efficiency. Maybe your old employer treated you badly, or you washed out. You may hope to use what you learned there to your advantage. Either way, you now bring your talents to the company.",
"bg|Ruined": "You once enjoyed luxury, love, and comfort, then lost everything. You may have been framed for crimes, had a monster wipe out your holdings, or drawn a destructive card from a Deck of Many Things. Desperation pushed you to adventuring because every other path closed. Fortune lifted you once, and it might again.",
"bg|Rune Carver": "You have devoted your life to runecraft, which giants first created and many peoples now use. A master may have taught you, or you may have learned from ancient engravings. You tap the power held in runes, usually Giant runes, though many carvers also use symbols from their own languages.",
"bg|Sage": "You spent years learning the lore of the multiverse. You searched through manuscripts, studied scrolls, and listened to the greatest experts on the topics that interest you. All that effort made you a master in your fields of study.",
"bg|Sailor": "You sailed on a seagoing ship for years and faced fierce storms, sea monsters, and enemies who wanted your vessel sunk. The distant horizon is your first love, yet you are ready to try something new. Talk with your DM about your ship, your duties, and how you left.",
"bg|Scribe": "You spent formative years in a scriptorium, a monastery that preserves knowledge, or a government office. There you learned to write with a clear hand and produce fine texts. You might write poetry, stories, or research. Above all you pay careful attention to detail, so your copies contain no mistakes.",
"bg|Seer Apprentice": "You apprenticed with the Seers of Sea and Sky and learned to read small omens in the clouds above and the depths below. Their rich network of libraries furthered your education. Now you travel the world and offer advice and aid to others.",
"bg|Selesnya Initiate": "You belong to a blessed community built on harmony, where nature and civilization live together by the will of the Worldsoul, Mat'Selesnya. In the Selesnya Conclave you share a longing for spiritual communion with the world. You want to spread that joy through Ravnica and resist rival guilds, by force if needed.",
"bg|Shadowmasters Exile": "You trained your whole life to join the Shadowmasters, the secretive thieves' guild that quietly rules Thesk. Beyond stealth and quick reflexes, you learned the ruthlessness needed to protect its secrets. One mistake got you expelled from the order, and now you walk your own path.",
}
